// ENTER constrained mode immediately with EnterObservedConstrainedSpan. Then
// CloseSpanWithinBudget exhausts the remaining budget on one parser-controlled span.
// The budget is consumed after close, so no second forced span can appear.
//
// Phase 0: Close any inherited open span (up to 20 steps via CloseSpanWithinBudget)
// Phase 1: Free unconstrained generation until "<<" detected (up to 85% of maxSteps)
//   - RenderedEndsWith(generated, "<<") triggers EnterObservedConstrainedSpan + break
// Phase 2: Force-open span ONLY if Phase 1 ended without detecting "<<"
// Phase 3: CloseSpanWithinBudget on all remaining budget
//   - Tracks LONGEST complete parse; emits ">>" there to prevent premature close
//   - Prevents short int(n) closes before the full expression is generated
//
// Guidance improvement: explicitly require preserving underscores in variable names
// (n_1 not n1) to fix symbolic evaluation mismatches that appeared in diagnostics.
// CSD_RATIONALE_END
// CSD_PROOF_SKETCH_BEGIN
// Invariant 1: parser_validity
//   insideConstrainedOut ==> parser.IsValidPrefix(currentConstrainedOut)
//
//   Phase 0 (CloseSpanWithinBudget): postcondition guarantees
//     insideOut ==> parser.IsValidPrefix(currentOut); invariant preserved.
//
//   Phase 1 loop — free generation branch (no "<<" detected):
